<!DOCTYPE html>
<html metal:use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/page"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
      xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
      xmlns:metal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/metal">

  <title metal:fill-slot="title">Equipment settings</title>
  <metal:fill fill-slot="header-title">Equipment settings</metal:fill>
  <tal:c metal:fill-slot="header-context"><span class="pfas-chip" tal:content="python:view.unit()['name']">Balance 1</span></tal:c>
  <tal:r metal:fill-slot="header-right">
    <a class="btn-sm btn-secondary" tal:attributes="href string:${view/portal_url}/@@pfas-equipment">&larr; Equipment</a>
    <a class="btn-sm btn-secondary" tal:attributes="href python:view.unit()['url'] + '/base_edit'">Edit in SENAITE</a>
  </tal:r>

  <!-- the form's Save, pinned at the foot of the window -->
  <tal:ab metal:fill-slot="action-bar"><tal:sb tal:condition="view/can_configure" tal:define="sb_form string:equipment-settings-form"><div
      metal:use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/save-bar"></div></tal:sb></tal:ab>

  <div metal:fill-slot="content">
  <div class="page-body-narrow" tal:define="u view/unit; kind u/unit_type">

    <div class="alert alert-success" tal:condition="view/saved">Saved.</div>
    <div class="alert alert-error" tal:condition="view/folder_refused">Not saved: use an absolute path.</div>
    <p class="form-note">
      <strong tal:content="u/name">Balance 1</strong>
      &middot; type <span tal:replace="u/type_title">Balance</span>
      <tal:s condition="u/serial_number">&middot; SN <span tal:replace="u/serial_number">123</span></tal:s>.
      Identity and certificates live in SENAITE; the PFAS check settings live here. <tal:h define="hid string:equipment-types"><metal:b use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/help" /></tal:h>
    </p>

    <form method="post" id="equipment-settings-form" tal:attributes="action string:${view/portal_url}/@@pfas-equipment-settings?uid=${u/id}">
      <input type="hidden" name="action" value="save" tal:condition="view/can_configure" />

      <tal:study condition="python:kind in ('thermometer', 'ir_gun', 'nitrogen_evaporator')">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Temperature study</div>
        <p class="form-note">Corrected to the NIST reference by its quarterly study; the factor in force applies wherever its readings are used. <tal:h define="hid string:temperature-study"><metal:b use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/help" /></tal:h></p>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Study tolerance per reading pair (&deg;C)</label>
            <input type="number" step="0.1" name="study_tolerance" tal:attributes="value u/study_tolerance" /></div>
          <div class="pfas-form-field" tal:condition="view/multi_point"><label for="es-wt">Working temperatures (&deg;C)</label>
            <input type="text" name="working_temps" id="es-wt" data-chips="list" placeholder="-20, 4, 20"
                   tal:attributes="value view/working_temps_text" /></div>
        </div>
      </tal:study>
      <p class="form-note" tal:condition="python:kind == 'reference_thermometer'">
        Checked externally: record its certificate in SENAITE; the certificate&rsquo;s valid-to date is its due date. <tal:h define="hid string:temperature-study"><metal:b use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/help" /></tal:h></p>

      <tal:temp condition="python:kind in ('refrigerator', 'freezer', 'water_bath', 'room_sensor')">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Temperature monitoring</div>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Sensor id</label>
            <input type="text" name="sensor_id" tal:attributes="value u/sensor_id" /></div>
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Temperature range (&deg;C)</label>
            <div data-range="data-range" data-scale="-90,40" data-unit="&#176;C">
              <input type="number" step="0.1" name="temp_min" aria-label="Temperature minimum" tal:attributes="value u/temp_min" />
              <input type="number" step="0.1" name="temp_max" aria-label="Temperature maximum" tal:attributes="value u/temp_max" /></div></div>
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Humidity range (%)</label>
            <div data-range="data-range" data-scale="0,100" data-unit="%">
              <input type="number" step="0.1" name="humidity_min" aria-label="Humidity minimum" tal:attributes="value u/humidity_min" />
              <input type="number" step="0.1" name="humidity_max" aria-label="Humidity maximum" tal:attributes="value u/humidity_max" /></div></div>
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Mapping study tolerance (&deg;C)</label>
            <input type="number" step="0.1" name="study_tolerance" tal:attributes="value u/study_tolerance" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-warning" tal:define="hc view/hold_conflict" tal:condition="hc" tal:content="hc">ranges do not overlap</div>
        <p class="form-note" tal:define="hr view/hold_range" tal:condition="hr" tal:content="hr">Judged at -20 to -10 °C</p>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field" tal:repeat="m view/kept_choices">
            <span class="pfas-label" tal:content="python:u'Holds, %s' % view.method_name(m['mid'])">Holds, EPA 537.1 Drinking Water</span>
            <div class="cf-chips">
              <label class="pfas-switch cf-chip" tal:repeat="k python:m['items']">
                <input type="checkbox" value="on" tal:attributes="name k/name; checked python:'checked' if k['on'] else None" /><span class="pfas-switch-track"></span>
                <span tal:replace="k/label">Samples</span></label>
            </div>
            <span class="pfas-label" tal:condition="m/matrices">Matrices held</span>
            <div class="cf-chips" tal:condition="m/matrices">
              <label class="pfas-switch cf-chip" tal:repeat="x m/matrices">
                <input type="checkbox" value="on" tal:attributes="name x/name; checked python:'checked' if x['on'] else None" /><span class="pfas-switch-track"></span>
                <span tal:replace="x/label">Soil</span></label>
            </div></div>
        </div>
      </tal:temp>

      <tal:bal condition="python:kind in ('balance_analytical', 'balance_prep')">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Weight points (g)</div>
        <p class="form-note">
          Acceptance is the type&rsquo;s tolerance:
          <strong tal:content="python:'%g %% of nominal' % u['tolerance_pct'] if u['tolerance_pct'] else 'not set'">0.2 % of nominal</strong>.
        </p>
        <table class="pfas-table pfas-table-form" data-col-resize="equipment-settings-1">
          <thead><tr><th>Nominal (g)</th><th>Label</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr tal:repeat="wp python:list(view.weight_points()) + [[None, u''], [None, u'']]">
              <td><input type="number" step="any"
                         tal:attributes="name string:wp_nominal_${repeat/wp/index};
                                         value python:'' if wp[0] is None else wp[0]" /></td>
              <td><input type="text" tal:attributes="name string:wp_label_${repeat/wp/index}; value python:wp[1]" /></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </tal:bal>

      <tal:water condition="python:kind == 'water_system'">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Water limits</div>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Maximum conductivity (&micro;S/cm)</label>
            <input type="number" step="0.01" name="conductivity_max" tal:attributes="value view/extra/conductivity_max|nothing" /></div>
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Maximum TOC (ppb)</label>
            <input type="number" step="1" name="toc_max" tal:attributes="value view/extra/toc_max|nothing" /></div>
        </div>
      </tal:water>

      <tal:pip condition="python:kind == 'pipette'">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Calibration limits</div>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label for="es-acc">Systematic error limit (&#177; %)</label>
            <input type="number" step="any" min="0" name="pipette_accuracy_pct" id="es-acc" tal:attributes="value u/pipette_accuracy_pct" /></div>
          <div class="pfas-form-field"><label for="es-cv">Random error limit (RSD %)</label>
            <input type="number" step="any" min="0" name="pipette_precision_cv" id="es-cv" tal:attributes="value u/pipette_precision_cv" /></div>
        </div>
      </tal:pip>

      <tal:spe condition="python:kind == 'spe_manifold'">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Ports</div>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field is-wide"><label for="es-ports">Ports</label>
            <input type="text" name="spe_ports" id="es-ports" data-chips="list" placeholder="1, 2, 3"
                   tal:attributes="value view/spe_ports_text" /></div>
        </div>
      </tal:spe>

      <tal:raw condition="python:kind == 'analytical'">
        <div class="section-group-hdr">Raw data</div>
        <div class="pfas-form-row">
          <div class="pfas-form-field is-wide"><label for="es-raw">Raw data folder, as mounted in the worker</label>
            <input type="text" name="raw_folder" id="es-raw" placeholder="/mnt/lcms/data/instrument-1"
                   tal:attributes="value u/raw_folder|nothing; disabled python:'disabled' if not view.can_configure() else None" /></div>
        </div>
      </tal:raw>

      <p class="form-note" tal:condition="python:kind in ('eyewash', 'other')">
        Nothing to set here for this kind; its type and certificates are in SENAITE.
      </p>

    </form>
  </div>
  </div>
</html>
